# Skyline uses Open-Meteo, which needs NO API key for non-commercial use, so this
# file is empty by default. If you swap in a keyed provider (OpenWeatherMap,
# WeatherAPI, Tomorrow.io, Mapbox, etc.), add the key here and copy this file to
# `.env` (which is gitignored). Vite only exposes vars prefixed with VITE_ to the
# client — and anything VITE_-prefixed ships to the browser, so it is NOT secret.
#
# For a key that must stay private, do NOT put it here. Route the request through
# a serverless function and read the key from a server-only env var set in your
# host's dashboard (Vercel/Netlify).
#
# Example (public, client-side key only):
# VITE_SOME_PROVIDER_KEY=your-key-here
